From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:36:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: check the MT6797 start temperature only at a
 fixed clock

The 55 C start check came from bring-up, before the GPU had a cooling device. A
Gemini booted warm after charging read 57 C, refused the GPU, and its desktop ran
the whole session without one.

With DVFS, the default, the cooling device and the SoC trips at 58 C and above
handle heat, so start regardless. Keep the check for the fixed clocks, which have no
cooling device.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mt6797.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mt6797.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mt6797.c
index 73c48b404..60dc25891 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mt6797.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mt6797.c
@@ -259,9 +259,16 @@ static int mt6797_power_early(struct panfrost_device *pfdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(rstc))
 		return PTR_ERR(rstc);
 
-	ret = mt6797_check_temperature(dev);
-	if (ret)
-		goto err_put_reset;
+	/*
+	 * A fixed clock has no cooling device, so it does not start on a hot SoC.
+	 * With DVFS the cooling device and the SoC's trips handle heat, and refusing
+	 * would leave a session started warm, as after charging, with no GPU.
+	 */
+	if (!mt6797_dvfs) {
+		ret = mt6797_check_temperature(dev);
+		if (ret)
+			goto err_put_reset;
+	}
 
 	if (mt6797_dvfs) {
 		/*
